      "id": 1,
      "text": "Richmond Hill was renamed from Ways Station after Henry Ford's home on the Ogeechee River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Richmond_Hill%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Henry Ford wintered there for nearly 25 years, leaving a legacy seen at the Richmond Hill History Museum and Driving Trail.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitrichmondhill.com/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits on the Ogeechee River fifteen miles south of Savannah and is the largest municipality in Bryan County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
